[
{
"content_id": "19672",
"reference_id": 18840,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jude 1:1",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "65001001",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Jude (or <em>Judas</em>) is the Greek version of the Hebrew name “Judah.” It was a common name. This Jude was a brother of James, who was also a brother of Jesus (see <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"Jude_BookIntro_Filament\" data-resource-code=\"AquiferOpenStudyNotes\">Jude Book Introduction</data>, “Author”). </p></li><li><p><span><em>a servant of Jesus Christ</em></span>: Jude states he follows Jesus in all parts of life. This title also shows honor. Important leaders in the Old Testament were called <em>slaves</em> or <em>servants</em> of God (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"06014007\" data-end-ref=\"06014007\">Joshua 14:7</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"12018012\" data-end-ref=\"12018012\">2&nbsp;Kings 18:12</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26034023\" data-end-ref=\"26034023\">Ezekiel 34:23</data>). </p></li><li><p><span><em>To those who are called</em></span>: We do not know exactly who Jude wrote this letter to.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
