"content_id": "19664",
"reference_id": 18832,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jude 1:1–2",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "65001001-65001002",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Following the typical structure of the beginning of a letter, Jude identifies himself, addresses his audience, and prays for them.</p></li><li><p><span><em>kept in Jesus Christ</em></span>: This phrase emphasizes an important point (see also <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"65001021\" data-end-ref=\"65001021\">1:21</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"65001024\" data-end-ref=\"65001024\">24</data>). It gives believers confidence when they face people who teach wrong things about God.</p></li></ul>",
