{
"content_id": "19678",
"reference_id": 18846,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jude 1:3–4",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "65001003-65001004",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>Instead of the usual thanksgiving that usually occurs at this point in New Testament letters, Jude explains his main purpose (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"45001008\" data-end-ref=\"45001014\">Romans 1:8–14</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"46001004\" data-end-ref=\"46001009\">1&nbsp;Corinthians 1:4–9</data>). False teaching was a serious threat to the faith of the people he was writing to (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"65001022\" data-end-ref=\"65001023\">Jude 1:22–23</data>).</p>",
"associations": {
