{
"content_id": "19684",
"reference_id": 18852,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jude 1:7",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "65001007",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>God&apos;s judgment on Sodom and Gomorrah became well-known (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"01018017\" data-end-ref=\"01019026\">Genesis 18:17–19:26</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"42017026\" data-end-ref=\"42017029\">Luke 17:26–29</data>). </p></li><li><p><span><em>the cities around them</em></span>: <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"05029023\" data-end-ref=\"05029023\">Deuteronomy 29:23</data> mentions Admah and Zeboiim. </p></li><li><p><span><em>sexual immorality and pursued strange flesh</em>: this likely refers to sexual relations between people of the same sex</span> (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"01019005\" data-end-ref=\"01019010\">Genesis 19:5–10</data>).</p></li></ul>",
