"title": "Jude 1:22–23",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "65001022-65001023",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>The Berean Standard Bible follows a manuscript tradition with three commands for different groups: </p><ol><li><p>those who doubt, </p></li><li><p>those needing rescue from judgment (&quot;by snatching them from the fire&quot;), and </p></li><li><p>those needing mercy. </p></li></ol><p>Some manuscripts mention only two groups: </p><ol><li><p>those with wavering faith who need rescue from judgment, and </p></li><li><p>those needing mercy. </p></li></ol><p>The Berean Standard Bible uses the three-part pattern found in other parts of Jude (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"65001005\" data-end-ref=\"65001007\">1:5–7</data>, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"65001011\" data-end-ref=\"65001011\">11</data>).</p>",
